From 68cd85e0bd695c46802203e178bfdfced657d646 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:39:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2149/2165] wifi: ath12k: avoid sleeping PCI wakeup during
 panic reset

The WCN7850 PCI panic callback reaches mhi_device_get_sync through its
register wakeup helper. An archived SP11 hung-task panic shows this
sleeping with preemption and interrupts disabled after other CPUs have
stopped, disrupting the dump path. Skip the panic-only reset on PCI
variants with a wakeup callback. Normal operation and recovery are
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit d6b13e3e295312d9549a76215771987034851ccd)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
index fee4129ea4055b4d84f4a9d812627a736669a045..b546910f046d218c77906b354a8f27a49b184685 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
@@ -1475,6 +1475,17 @@ void ath12k_pci_power_down(struct ath12k_base *ab, bool is_suspend)
 
 static int ath12k_pci_panic_handler(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
+	struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci = ath12k_pci_priv(ab);
+
+	/*
+	 * Register accesses on devices with a wakeup callback can wait for
+	 * MHI, which sleeps. Panic notifiers run with interrupts disabled
+	 * after the other CPUs have stopped, so such a reset can prevent
+	 * the kernel from reaching its crash dump handlers.
+	 */
+	if (ab_pci->pci_ops->wakeup)
+		return NOTIFY_DONE;
+
 	ath12k_pci_sw_reset(ab, false);
 
 	return NOTIFY_OK;
